        "corner_radius": 32,
        "corner_radius_mobile": 16,
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "",
        "text": "<p>My mother used to make my frocks.</p><p>She would choose the fabrics, stitch them herself and add little embroidered details. I grew up wearing clothes made by her hands, long before I understood how much time, thought and skill went into them.</p><p>Perhaps that's where it all began.</p><p>I learnt my first crochet stitch when I was six or seven. Before long, the entire family had crochet caps made by me.</p><p>Then came embroidered table covers, clothes for my dolls, and eventually, clothes for myself.</p><p>I learnt to sew on my mother's old Usha foot-pedal machine.</p><p>That sewing machine still sits in my office today.</p>",
        "text_font": "heading",
        "text_style": "body",
        "show_rule": false,
