        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "A life spent around cloth",
        "text": "<p>When it came to choosing what I wanted to study, textiles and fashion felt like a natural continuation of everything I had grown up with.</p><p>I found myself drawn to natural fabrics. Cotton, linen, silk. I loved the character of each material and the possibilities of Indian textile crafts.</p><p>Over the years, my work took me into a much larger world of clothing and home textiles.</p><p>I designed and produced for international clients and learnt the disciplines of manufacturing, quality, production and global trade.</p><p>It was a very different world from my mother's sewing machine, but fabric remained at the centre of it.</p>",
        "text_font": "heading",
        "text_style": "body",
        "show_rule": false,
