        "corner_radius_mobile": 16,
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Finding my own way",
        "text": "<p>After spending so much of my life making things for others, I began reflecting on my own journey.</p><p>On how much life changes as we grow older. The roles we play, the responsibilities we carry, the unexpected turns, and the things we slowly learn to value.</p><p>Somewhere in those reflections, Tabi took shape.</p><p><em>Tabi</em> is the Japanese word for journey.</p><p>For me, it represents our passage through life, with all its challenges, surprises and beautiful moments.</p><p>And perhaps, eventually, arriving at a place where we begin to appreciate things a little differently.</p><p>The quiet of an early morning. The changing colour of leaves. River stones softened by time. The feeling of a beautiful natural fabric against the skin.</p><p>The things that ask for our attention without demanding it.</p>",
        "text_font": "heading",
        "text_style": "body",
        "show_rule": false,
        "button_label": "",
        "text_align": "left",
        "text_align_mobile": "left",
        "motion": true,
